# SONiC ZTP (Zero Touch Provisioning) — End-to-End Architecture

> Source-grounded design document derived strictly from `src/sonic-ztp` in this repo
> plus its integration points in `files/`, `rules/`, `slave.mk`, and `sonic-yang-models`.
> Diagrams are written in **Mermaid** — paste the ```mermaid blocks into GitHub, VS Code,
> mermaid.live, or Confluence to render them.

---

## 0. What ZTP is, in one paragraph (from the code)

ZTP is a **boot-time daemon** (`ztp.service` → `/usr/lib/ztp/ztp-engine.py`) that runs *only when a switch boots with no saved configuration*. It temporarily loads a minimal "ZTP profile" config that brings up management (`eth0`) and front-panel (`Ethernet*`) ports as DHCP clients, uses DHCP options to **discover a URL** pointing to provisioning instructions (a "ZTP JSON" file, or a script, or a minigraph), downloads them, and executes an ordered list of **plugins** ("configuration sections") that actually configure the device (load `config_db.json`, load a minigraph, install firmware, set SNMP, etc.). When done it removes the temporary profile so the real configuration takes over. It is packaged from the `src/sonic-ztp` git submodule and gated at image-build time by the `ENABLE_ZTP=y` make flag.

