## 3. The core engine (`ztp-engine.py` → class `ZTPEngine`)

The daemon is a single loop, `executeLoop()`. Its whole life is a **discovery loop** followed by **JSON processing** followed by **profile cleanup**.

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Init
  Init --> AdminCheck: updateActivity("Initializing")
  AdminCheck --> RemoveProfile: admin-mode == False
  RemoveProfile --> [*]
  AdminCheck --> DISCOVERY: admin-mode == True

  state DISCOVERY {
    [*] --> discover
    discover --> found: __discover() True
    discover --> notfound: False
    notfound --> loadProfile: __loadZTPProfile("discovery")
    loadProfile --> linkscan: __link_scan()
    linkscan --> restartIfc: link up detected → systemctl restart interfaces-config
    linkscan --> timercheck: no link up
    timercheck --> restartIfc2: elapsed > restart-ztp-interval (300s)
    timercheck --> sleep: else sleep(discovery-interval 10s)
    restartIfc --> discover
    restartIfc2 --> discover
    sleep --> discover
  }

  found --> MANUAL_CONFIG: minigraph.xml / config_db.json / warm boot
  found --> processJSON: ztp_mode != DISCOVERY
  MANUAL_CONFIG --> RemoveProfile2
  processJSON --> retry: rv=retry → back to DISCOVERY
  processJSON --> restart: rv=restart → __forceRestartDiscovery
  processJSON --> RemoveProfile2: rv=stop
  retry --> DISCOVERY
  restart --> DISCOVERY
  RemoveProfile2 --> RebootMaybe: reboot_on_completion?
  RebootMaybe --> [*]
```

Key engine methods (all in `ztp-engine.py`):

| Method | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| `executeLoop()` | Top-level loop; admin-mode gate; discovery; profile removal; final reboot. |
| `__discover()` | Precedence-ordered detection of provisioning source (§6). Sets `ztp_mode`. |
| `__loadZTPProfile(event)` | Calls `ztp-profile.sh install <discovery\|resume>` once (`__ztp_profile_loaded` guard). |
| `__removeZTPProfile()` | Calls `ztp-profile.sh remove [config-fallback]`; strips `ZTP` key from `config_db.json`. |
| `__processZTPJson()` | Loads `ZTPJson`, marks start, runs sections, evaluates result, decides restart/stop. |
| `__processConfigSections()` | Iterates sorted sections; resolves + runs plugin; maps exit code → SUCCESS/SUSPEND/FAILED; handles `halt-on-failure`. |
| `__evalZTPResult()` | Overall SUCCESS/FAILED from section results + `ignore-result`; delayed reboot. |
| `__rebootAction()` | Honors `reboot-on-success` / `reboot-on-failure`. |
| `__link_scan()` / `__detect_intf_state()` | Watches `/sys/class/net/*/operstate` and APPL_DB `PORT_TABLE` for a port coming up, to retrigger DHCP. |
| `__downloadURL()` | Reads a URL-file (written by DHCP hook), downloads via `Downloader`, records the discovering interface. |
| `__createProvScriptJson()` / `__createGraphserviceJson()` | Synthesize a ZTP JSON wrapper for the Option-239 script and Option-225/226 minigraph cases. |
| `__forceRestartDiscovery()` | Clears DHCP leases, sleeps `restart-ztp-interval`, forces profile reload + link rescan. |

`signal_handler` (SIGTERM/SIGINT) waits up to `sighandler-wait-interval` (60s) for child plugin PIDs (`runcmd_pids`) then SIGKILLs them — this is how `systemctl stop ztp` cleanly aborts a running plugin.

