## 4. The data model

### 4.1 The three JSON files (in `/host/ztp/`)

- **`ztp_cfg.json`** (`getCfg('...')` config) — daemon tunables; every key + default is in `defaults.py`. Only `admin-mode` is persisted by default; everything else falls back to `defaultCfg`.
- **`ztp_data.json`** (`ztp-json`) — the *working* ZTP JSON: full provisioning instructions + live per-section status. This is the source of truth for a session.
- **`ztp_data_shadow.json`** (`ztp-json-shadow`) — a **sanitized** copy (mode `0644`) containing only `['ignore-result','reboot-on-success','reboot-on-failure','halt-on-failure','description','timestamp','status','start-timestamp','error']` per section. URLs, plugin bodies, and credentials are stripped. The `ztp status` CLI reads *only* the shadow file.

### 4.2 ZTP JSON structure (parsed by `ZTPSections.ZTPJson`)

```jsonc
{
  "ztp": {
    // optional: whole file can itself be fetched via a url/dynamic-url
    "url": { "source": "http://server/ztp.json" },

    // global flags (defaults come from ztp_cfg.json)
    "ignore-result": false,
    "restart-ztp-on-failure": false,
    "restart-ztp-no-config": true,
    "config-fallback": false,
    "reboot-on-success": false,
    "reboot-on-failure": false,

    // one or more "configuration sections":
    "01-firmware":     { "plugin": "firmware",    "install": {} },
    "02-configdb-json":{ "plugin": {"url": {}}, "clear-config": true },
    "09-provisioning": {
        "plugin": { "url": {"source":"http://s/p.sh"}, "shell": true },
        "suspend-exit-code": 2,
        "halt-on-failure": true
    }
  }
}
```

**How sections turn into work** (`ZTPJson.__init__`):
1. If the top-level `ztp` has a `url`/`dynamic-url`, download the real JSON first and reload.
2. `__buildDefaults()` injects missing flags from config; validates `status`.
3. On first run (`status == BOOT`) `__cleanup()` wipes `/var/lib/ztp/{tmp,sections}`.
4. Each dict-valued key = a **configuration section**. `__writeConfigSections()` splits it into `/var/lib/ztp/sections/<name>/input.json` (`section-input-file`).
5. `plugin(name)` resolves the executable; `pluginArgs(name)` builds the argv.

**Plugin resolution order** (`ZTPJson.plugin()`):
```
plugin is dict?
 ├─ reuse /var/lib/ztp/sections/<sec>/plugin if already downloaded
 ├─ has "dynamic-url" → DynamicURL(...).download()   (identifier-templated URL)
 ├─ has "url"         → URL(...).download()
 └─ has "name"        → name
plugin is string → name = that string
no name → strip leading "NN-" from section name (regex ^[0-9]+-)
final → /usr/lib/ztp/plugins/<name>  (must exist, else None → section FAILED)
```
`pluginArgs()`: unless `ignore-section-data:true`, the first arg is the section's `input.json` path; an optional `args` string is appended. So the canonical invocation is:
```
/usr/lib/ztp/plugins/configdb-json  /var/lib/ztp/sections/02-configdb-json/input.json
```

### 4.3 Status state machines

**Configuration-section status** (enforced in `ConfigSection.__buildDefaults`; driven by `__processConfigSections`):

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> BOOT: section created
  BOOT --> IN_PROGRESS: engine picks it up
  SUSPEND --> IN_PROGRESS: retried next pass/boot
  IN_PROGRESS --> SUCCESS: plugin rc == 0
  IN_PROGRESS --> SUSPEND: rc == suspend-exit-code
  IN_PROGRESS --> FAILED: any other rc / exception / plugin unresolved
  BOOT --> DISABLED: invalid status value in JSON
  DISABLED --> [*]: skipped (ignored in result)
  SUCCESS --> [*]
  FAILED --> [*]
  note right of FAILED
    halt-on-failure:true → abort whole run
    reboot-on-failure:true → reboot
  end note
```
Valid states: `BOOT, IN-PROGRESS, SUSPEND, DISABLED, FAILED, SUCCESS`.

**Overall ZTP status** (`__evalZTPResult`, shown by `ztp status -c`):
```
0:DISABLED  admin-mode == False
3:NOT-STARTED (BOOT)  →  4:IN-PROGRESS  →  5:SUCCESS | 6:FAILED
(2:ACTIVE-DISCOVERY if service up but no shadow JSON yet; 1:INACTIVE otherwise)
```
Result rule: ZTP = SUCCESS unless some section is `FAILED` with `ignore-result:false`; global `ignore-result:true` forces SUCCESS. `DISABLED` sections are ignored.

### 4.4 Config keys (selected — full list is `defaults.py`, 55+ keys)

| Key | Default | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `admin-mode` | `True` | Master on/off (the only persisted key). |
| `feat-inband` / `feat-ipv4` / `feat-ipv6` | `True` | Enable in-band ports / IPv4 / IPv6 discovery. |
| `discovery-interval` | `10` | Sleep between discovery passes. |
| `restart-ztp-interval` | `300` | Restart networking if no data found in this window. |
| `restart-ztp-on-failure` | `False` | Re-run ZTP if it ends FAILED. |
| `restart-ztp-no-config` | `True` | Re-run ZTP if it ends with no `config_db.json`. |
| `restart-ztp-on-invalid-data` | `True` | Re-discover if downloaded JSON is invalid. |
| `monitor-startup-config` | `True` | Presence of `config_db.json` means "provisioned". |
| `config-fallback` | `False` | On removal, load startup/factory config. |
| `curl-retries`/`curl-timeout` | `3`/`30` | Download behavior. |
| `opt67-url`, `opt59-v6-url`, `opt239-url`, `opt239-v6-url`, `opt66-tftp-server`, `graph-url`, `acl-url` | `/var/run/ztp/...` | Files the DHCP hook writes discovered URLs into. |
| `ztp-json`, `ztp-json-shadow`, `ztp-json-local` | `/host/ztp/...` | Working / shadow / operator-supplied JSON. |
| `plugins-dir` | `/usr/lib/ztp/plugins` | Built-in plugin lookup. |

