## 5. Boot integration — how ZTP actually starts

`config-setup` (`files/image_config/config-setup/config-setup`) decides at first boot whether ZTP runs at all:

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  A["config-setup: do_config_initialization()"] --> B{minigraph.xml present?}
  B -- yes --> C["reload_minigraph → NOT ZTP"]
  B -- no --> D{ztp_is_enabled?<br/>ztp status -c != 0:DISABLED}
  D -- no --> E["factory default preset config"]
  D -- yes --> F["ztp-profile.sh create → /tmp/ztp_config_db.json<br/>reload_configdb (loads ZTP profile)"]
  F --> G["ztp.service starts (After config-setup)"]
  A --> W{warm boot?}
  W -- yes --> X["skip config init & ZTP entirely"]
```

Then `ztp.service` (`After=config-setup.service interfaces-config.service rsyslog-config.service`) launches `/usr/lib/ztp/sonic-ztp` → `ztp-engine.py`.

The **ZTP profile** that `ztp-profile.sh` loads (rendered from `ztp-config.j2`) is a `config_db.json` containing:
- `DEVICE_METADATA.localhost.type = "not-provisioned"`, hostname `sonic`
- full `PORT` table, `admin_status: up` for front-panel ports **iff** `ZTP_INBAND=="true"` (else `down`)
- `ZTP|mode` = `{profile:"active", inband, out-of-band:"true", ipv4, ipv6, product-name, serial-no}`

`ZTP|mode.profile == "active"` is the single flag every other component keys off (`ztp-profile.sh get_ztp_profile`, engine `__is_ztp_profile_active`, `configdb-json __stop_dhcp`, `interfaces.j2`, `graphserviceurl`).

The rendered ConfigDB profile drives `interfaces.j2` / `dhclient.conf.j2` (in `files/`) to emit DHCP stanzas: `eth0` unconditionally (v4/v6 per flags), and each in-band `Ethernet*` port whose live `oper_status == up`. `dhclient.conf.j2` also requests the special options and sends `user-class "SONiC-ZTP"` and `dhcp-client-identifier "SONiC##<product>##<serial>"`.

