## 6. Discovery precedence (`__discover()`)

The engine checks these in strict order and stops at the first hit:

```
1. /host/ztp/ztp_data.json exists         → resume existing session (ztp-session)
2. warm boot (/proc/cmdline)              → MANUAL_CONFIG (skip)
3. /etc/sonic/minigraph.xml exists        → MANUAL_CONFIG (skip)
4. /etc/sonic/config_db.json exists       → MANUAL_CONFIG (skip)   [monitor-startup-config]
5. /host/ztp/ztp_data_local.json          → local-fs
6. DHCP Option 67 URL   (+ Option 66 tftp server prefix)  → dhcp-opt67
7. DHCPv6 Option 59 URL                   → dhcp6-opt59
8. DHCP Option 239 provisioning-script URL→ dhcp-opt239   (wraps script into ZTP JSON)
9. DHCPv6 Option 239 URL                  → dhcp6-opt239
10. DHCP Option 225 minigraph URL (+226 ACL) → dhcp-opt225-graph-url (wraps into graphservice JSON)
```

The DHCP hook `/usr/lib/ztp/dhcp/ztp` is what populates the files in steps 6–10, writing `$new_bootfile_name`→opt67 file, `$new_tftp_server_name`→opt66 file, `$new_dhcp6_boot_file_url`→opt59 file, `$new_provisioning_script_url`→opt239 file, `$new_minigraph_url`→graph file, `$new_acl_url`→acl file — guarded by a per-interface/per-proto lock (`/var/run/ztp/ztp.lock`) and only when `ztp status -c != 0:DISABLED`.

