## 7. Sequence diagrams — every supported use-case

### 7.1 Fresh boot, no data yet → in-band link-scan discovery loop

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant SD as systemd
  participant ENG as ztp-engine
  participant PS as ztp-profile.sh
  participant DB as CONFIG_DB
  participant DHC as dhclient
  participant HK as dhcp hooks
  SD->>ENG: start (After config-setup/interfaces/rsyslog)
  ENG->>ENG: admin-mode == True
  loop DISCOVERY
    ENG->>ENG: __discover() → no source yet
    ENG->>PS: install discovery
    PS->>DB: config reload /tmp/ztp_config_db.json (ZTP profile, ports admin up)
    PS->>PS: wait_for_system_online (ports appear)
    DHC->>HK: enter-hook inband-ztp-ip(6) → config interface ip add EthernetX
    DHC->>HK: exit-hook ztp → write /var/run/ztp/dhcp_67-ztp_data_url
    ENG->>ENG: __link_scan(): operstate up on EthernetX?
    alt link up detected
      ENG->>SD: systemctl restart interfaces-config (re-run DHCP)
    else nothing for 300s
      ENG->>ENG: cleanup leases, restart interfaces-config
    else
      ENG->>ENG: sleep(discovery-interval 10s)
    end
  end
```

### 7.2 DHCP Option 67 (ZTP JSON URL), optional Option 66 (TFTP server)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant DHC as dhclient(eth0)
  participant HK as exit-hook ztp
  participant ENG as ztp-engine
  participant DL as Downloader(curl)
  participant SEC as ZTPJson
  participant PL as plugin(s)
  DHC->>HK: BOUND (new_bootfile_name, [new_tftp_server_name])
  HK->>HK: write dhcp_67-ztp_data_url (+ dhcp_66-ztp_tftp_server)
  ENG->>ENG: __discover(): opt67-url file present
  ENG->>DL: __downloadURL(opt67-url → ztp_data_opt67.json)<br/>prefix tftp://server/ if opt66 set
  DL-->>ENG: 0, file (records discovering interface)
  ENG->>ENG: mode=dhcp-opt67; __loadZTPProfile("resume")
  ENG->>SEC: ZTPJson(ztp_data_opt67.json → ztp_data.json)
  SEC->>SEC: split sections → /var/lib/ztp/sections/*/input.json; write shadow
  loop each section (sorted)
    ENG->>SEC: plugin(sec), pluginArgs(sec)
    ENG->>PL: run plugin input.json
    PL-->>ENG: rc → SUCCESS/SUSPEND/FAILED
  end
  ENG->>ENG: __evalZTPResult() → SUCCESS/FAILED
  ENG->>ENG: __removeZTPProfile()
```

### 7.3 DHCPv6 Option 59

Identical to 7.2 but source = `opt59-v6-url` → `ztp_data_opt59.json`, mode `dhcp6-opt59`, no TFTP prefix.

### 7.4 DHCP/DHCPv6 Option 239 — simple provisioning script

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant HK as exit-hook ztp
  participant ENG as ztp-engine
  participant DL as Downloader
  participant PL as plugin (download/execute script)
  HK->>HK: write dhcp_239-provisioning-script_url
  ENG->>DL: __downloadURL(opt239-url → /host/ztp/provisioning-script)
  ENG->>ENG: __createProvScriptJson() writes ztp_data.json:<br/>{provisioning-script:{plugin:{url:"file:///host/ztp/provisioning-script",ignore-section-data:true}}, restart-ztp-no-config:false}
  ENG->>PL: run the script as a section plugin
  PL-->>ENG: rc → result
```
The script is wrapped as a section whose plugin is the script itself (`ignore-section-data:true`, so it gets no argv). DHCPv6 Option 239 is the same via `opt239-v6-url`.

### 7.5 DHCP Option 225/226 — minigraph + ACL

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant HK as exit-hook ztp
  participant ENG as ztp-engine
  participant DL as Downloader
  participant GS as graphservice plugin
  participant CFG as config load_minigraph
  HK->>HK: write dhcp_graph_url (225) [+ dhcp_acl_url (226)]
  ENG->>DL: __createGraphserviceJson(): test-download graph (+acl), then write ztp_data.json:<br/>{graphservice:{minigraph-url:{url:...}[,acl-url:{url:...}]}, restart-ztp-no-config:false}
  ENG->>GS: run graphservice plugin
  GS->>DL: download → /etc/sonic/minigraph.xml (+ /etc/sonic/acl.json)
  GS->>CFG: config load_minigraph -y
  GS->>CFG: config save -y
  GS-->>ENG: exit rc
```

### 7.6 Local ZTP JSON file

`ztp_data_local.json` — same processing path as 7.2, no DHCP; `__updateZTPMode('local-fs', ...)`.

### 7.7 Config application via `configdb-json` plugin (the common path)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant ENG as ztp-engine
  participant P as configdb-json plugin
  participant DB as CONFIG_DB
  participant CFG as config CLI
  ENG->>P: run input.json
  P->>P: download url/dynamic-url → /tmp/config_dl.json
  P->>P: __sanitize_config: keep running platform/hwsku/mac unless overwrite-device-metadata
  P->>DB: ZTP|mode profile==active? → mod_entry("ZTP","mode",None)
  P->>CFG: systemctl restart interfaces-config (stop ZTP DHCP)
  alt clear-config (default)
    P->>CFG: config reload -f -y config_db.json
  else incremental
    P->>CFG: config load -y config_db.json
  end
  opt save-config
    P->>CFG: config save -y
  end
  P-->>ENG: exit 0 / rc
```

### 7.8 SUSPEND / retry semantics (e.g. wait-for-server, `test-plugin`, `connectivity-check`)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant ENG as ztp-engine
  participant P as plugin
  Note over ENG,P: section has "suspend-exit-code": N
  ENG->>P: run
  P-->>ENG: exit N  → section = SUSPEND
  ENG->>ENG: continue other sections; loop re-scans
  ENG->>P: run again (BOOT/SUSPEND re-picked as IN-PROGRESS)
  P-->>ENG: exit 0 → SUCCESS  (or other rc → FAILED)
```
`__processConfigSections` re-loops while any section is still `IN-PROGRESS`/re-queued; a SUSPENDed section is retried on the next pass and across reboots (it persists in `ztp_data.json`).

### 7.9 Firmware install with reboot

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant ENG as ztp-engine
  participant FW as firmware plugin
  participant SI as sonic-installer
  ENG->>FW: run (install:{url,version,set-default,...})
  FW->>FW: install.status==SUCCESS? → skip (idempotent across reboot)
  opt pre-check
    FW->>FW: download+run pre-check; non-zero → abort op
  end
  FW->>SI: list (Current/Next/Available)
  FW->>FW: download image; sonic-installer binary-version == version?
  FW->>SI: sonic-installer install -y image
  FW->>FW: rewrite ztp_data.json: install.status="SUCCESS"
  FW->>FW: systemReboot()  (unless skip-reboot/reboot-on-success)
  Note over ENG,FW: after reboot, engine resumes; section already SUCCESS
```

### 7.10 Result evaluation, restart & reboot decisions (end of `__processZTPJson`)

```mermaid
flowchart TD
  A["__evalZTPResult()"] --> B{ignore-result?}
  B -- yes --> S["overall SUCCESS"]
  B -- no --> C{any section FAILED & !ignore-result?}
  C -- yes --> F["overall FAILED"]
  C -- no --> S
  S --> R1{restart-ztp-no-config &&<br/>no config_db.json && !config-fallback?}
  F --> R2{restart-ztp-on-failure?}
  R1 -- yes --> RESTART["delete ztp_data.json → __forceRestartDiscovery"]
  R2 -- yes --> RESTART
  R1 -- no --> STOP["stop → __removeZTPProfile"]
  R2 -- no --> STOP
  STOP --> RB{reboot-on-success/failure set?}
  RB -- yes --> REBOOT["systemReboot()"]
  RB -- no --> DONE["exit service"]
```

### 7.11 Invalid downloaded JSON

`ZTPJson(...)` raises `ValueError` → engine deletes `ztp_data.json`/shadow → if `restart-ztp-on-invalid-data` (default True) returns `("restart", ...)` → `__forceRestartDiscovery` (clear leases, wait 300s, rescan); else stop.

### 7.12 Operator CLI use-cases (`/usr/bin/ztp`)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant U as operator
  participant CLI as ztp CLI
  participant SD as systemd
  participant PS as ztp-profile.sh
  U->>CLI: ztp run -y
  CLI->>CLI: admin-mode? erase session; rename config_db.json.<ts>
  CLI->>SD: systemctl start ztp
  U->>CLI: ztp disable -y
  CLI->>SD: systemctl stop ztp
  CLI->>CLI: setCfg admin-mode=False
  CLI->>PS: ztp-profile.sh remove config-fallback (load startup/factory)
  U->>CLI: ztp erase -y
  CLI->>SD: stop ztp; rm ztp_data.json + shadow
  U->>CLI: ztp status [-v|-c]
  CLI->>CLI: read shadow JSON → print overall + per-section
  U->>CLI: ztp enable
  CLI->>CLI: setCfg admin-mode=True (file only; no service start)
```

| Command | Root? | Effect |
|---|---|---|
| `ztp enable` | yes | `admin-mode=True` in `ztp_cfg.json` only. |
| `ztp disable [-y]` | yes | Stop service, `admin-mode=False`, `ztp-profile.sh remove config-fallback`. |
| `ztp run [-y]` | yes | Erase session, rename existing `config_db.json`, start service (fresh ZTP). |
| `ztp erase [-y]` | yes | Stop service, delete `ztp_data.json` + shadow. |
| `ztp status` / `-v` / `-c` | no | Terse / detailed / coded status from shadow JSON. |
| `ztp features` / `-v` | no | List `feat-*` capabilities compiled into the image. |

